    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Howley Souhan are delighted to introduce 25 Fergus Road to the market. This attractive three-bedroom mid-terrace home enjoys a highly sought-after location just a couple of minutes from the centre of Terenure Village.  With its generous bedroom accommodation, off-street parking, high ceilings, south-facing rear garden and immediate proximity to the village centre, this property is sure to appeal to a wide range of purchasers.\r\n\r\nAccommodation briefly comprises of entrance hallway with understairs storage, interconnecting living and dining rooms, kitchen and small utility space on the ground floor. The first floor comprises three bedrooms and spacious family bathroom.\r\n\r\nOne of the property's standout features is the south-facing rear garden, which has been finished in cobblelock and includes a timber shed, outside sink, yard toilet and covered area to the rear, offering considerable versatility and storage potential. The sunny south-facing aspect makes this an ideal space for outdoor entertaining, gardening or simply enjoying the sunshine.\r\n\r\nTo the front, the property benefits from off-street parking, a particularly valuable feature in this popular residential location.\r\n\r\nThe location is undoubtedly one of the property's greatest attractions. Situated just a short stroll from the centre of Terenure Village, placing a superb range of shops, cafés, restaurants, pubs and everyday amenities within easy reach.\r\n\r\nTerenure is renowned for its strong community atmosphere, excellent selection of schools and abundance of recreational facilities. The area also offers easy access to one of Dublin's most popular parks and green spaces, Bushy Park, while excellent transport links provide convenient access to the city centre and surrounding suburbs.\r\n\r\nThe property is also within easy reach of Rathgar, Harold's Cross, Templeogue and Rathfarnham, making it an ideal base for commuters and families alike."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Ground Floor:\r\n\r\nHallway: 4.06m x 1387m Spacious hallway with understairs storage spaces.\r\n\r\nLiving Room: 3.82m x 3.42m To the front with bay window.  Coving.  Feature fireplace.  Interconnecting doors to:\r\n\r\nDining Room: 3.77m x 3.27m To the rear with coving and patio doors to rear garden.\r\n\r\nKitchen: 2.53m x 2.4m Eye and floor level units with fridge freezer, dishwasher, electric oven and hob and extractor hood.  Door to small utility space with shelves and washing machine.  Door to rear garden.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor:\r\n\r\nBedroom One: 3.44m x 3.00m  To the front with bay window.  Wall to wall wardrobes.\r\n\r\nBedroom Two: 3.77m x 2.99m To the rear with wall to wall built in wardrobes.\r\n\r\nBedroom Three: 2.47m x 2.15m With built in wardrobe.\r\n\r\nBathroom: 2.62m  2.13m With three piece white suite. Fully tiled walls and floor. Electric shower.  Chrome radiator.  Hot press.  Window for natural light and ventilation.\r\n\r\nOutside:\r\n\r\nRear Garden:  Easily maintained cobblelock garden with timber shed, sink unit and tap, covered area and outside toilet room housing the gas boiler.\r\n\r\nFront Garden: Off street parking with cobblelock driveway."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Approx: 92 sq.m.\r\nHighly sought after Terenure location\r\nSouth facing rear garden\r\nGas fired radiator central heating\r\nDouble glazed windows\r\nInterconnecting reception rooms\r\nThree generously proportioned bedrooms\r\nOff-street parking\r\nShort walk to Bushy Park\r\nClose to a variety of shops, schools, recreational sports and clubs and numerous transport links."
      },
      {
